        "Net-(J2-Pin_3)",
        "Net-(J5-Pin_3)",
        "/NET0030"
      ],
      "observed": "The netlist and SPICE deck show all six 0 Ω mode-selection jumpers shorted: R1 and R6 connect M-BUS pins 22 and 20 together through /NET0041; R9 and R23 connect M-BUS pins 21 and 19 together through /NET0009; R2 bridges the two servo signal pins; and R20 connects the servo signal node to U2 A.",
      "expected": "The specification states that PWM and serial servo modes are mutually exclusive and selected by populating different 0 Ω jumpers. A valid PWM build should leave the serial bridge jumpers open, and a valid serial build should not leave both alternative PWM-selection jumpers shorted; at most the appropriate PWM selection jumper(s) should be populated for the intended mode.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R1 /NET0041 /NET0002 0"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R6 /NET0041 /NET0016 0"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R9 /NET0009 /NET0014 0"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R23 /NET0009 /NET0018 0"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R2 Net-_J5-Pin_3_ Net-_J2-Pin_3_ 0"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R20 /NET0030 Net-_J5-Pin_3_ 0"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two mutually-exclusive servo interface modes, selected at assembly time by populating different 0 Ω jumper resistors"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "PWM mode (populate R3/R4, and the appropriate R9–R12 pair for the Core variant; leave R13/R14 open)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Short R13, R14 for Serial Servo"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The PWM GPIO selection nets and the serial servo bus are merged. This can short two M5Stack bus GPIO pins together and load the serial bus with PWM GPIO lines, causing bus contention, incorrect servo behavior, and possible damage if the GPIOs are driven.",
      "confidence": 0.75
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show all mode-selecting 0 Ω jumpers shorted, which contradicts the specification's mutually exclusive PWM/serial jumper configuration and creates unintended bridges between M-BUS GPIO pins and the serial servo bus."
}

